The patch fixes the bug by ensuring that when an error is detected in `xfrm_expand_policies()`, the `num_pols` is set to 0. This prevents `xfrm_bundle_lookup()` from calling `xfrm_pols_put()` on an invalid or already freed reference, thus avoiding both the double free and illegal memory access issues.


